          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="notes" value="&lt;b&gt;Design notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#10;• API is stateless — it writes a run row, publishes run_id to SQS, returns 202. It never blocks on the transform.&lt;br&gt;&#10;• Standard queue, not FIFO: event order is recovered from the timestamp column inside the payload, so per-group throughput limits buy nothing.&lt;br&gt;&#10;• At-least-once delivery — the worker is idempotent (upsert keyed on object_id, run claimed via conditional update).&lt;br&gt;&#10;• Single datastore: run state and transformed output both live in Postgres so they can be joined. DynamoDB was considered and rejected for that reason.&lt;br&gt;&#10;• Message carries an S3 key, not the payload — keeps the queue small and the API free of data handling.&lt;br&gt;&#10;• Private subnets reach S3/SQS/ECR/Logs through VPC endpoints; no NAT gateway needed for the data path.&lt;br&gt;&#10;• &lt;i&gt;Simplified in Terraform:&lt;/i&gt; single AZ, no WAF, no Route 53 zone, no autoscaling policies, RDS single-instance." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fillColor=#F8F8F8;strokeColor=#B3B3B3;fontSize=11;fontColor=#232F3E;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="860" y="880" width="480" height="180" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
